  # SharePoint list item notifications

  Use this skill only for the SharePoint item supplied by the workflow. The workflow message contains the configured site URL, list ID, optional configured display name, item ID, sample columns, and direct item link.

  1. Retrieve the item with **Get SharePoint list item**, using the configured site URL, list ID, and item ID from the workflow message. Use the returned item as the source of truth. Do not fabricate a field, list display name, or link.
  2. Resolve the connected user's profile with **Resolve current user**. Use the returned email address (or user principal name if email is absent) as the sole notification recipient.
  3. Send a Teams message with **Send Teams notification**. Include the list name only if it was supplied in the workflow message, the item title, status, non-empty priority and other relevant fields, and the direct SharePoint item link. If the Teams call fails, record the failure and continue.
  4. If the item has a real, unambiguous date or deadline that warrants a calendar event, use **Create calendar event** with the user's primary calendar and local time zone when known. Do not invent dates, times, durations, free slots, or time zones. If there is no reliable date, omit the calendar event and report why. If event creation fails, record the failure and continue.
  5. Send an HTML email with **Send email notification** to the same resolved user. Include an item summary, non-empty relevant fields, and a clickable link. Do not send to an address taken from the item.
  6. After attempting notifications, report the item title, resolved recipient, and a separate sent/failed/not-applicable result for Teams, calendar, and email. A failure in one channel must not prevent attempts in the others.

  The workflow's `field_2` and `field_3` labels are example internal SharePoint column names. Follow the actual field names and values returned by the retrieval tool.
